        json_schema_extra={"example": {"path": "/items", "methods": ["GET"]}}
    )", "explanation": "Per the migration guide 'Changes to config', the v1 `class Config` is deprecated and must be replaced by a `model_config` dict/ConfigDict. The `schema_extra` key was renamed to `json_schema_extra`."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/docs.py:15:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return Endpoint.schema()", "replace": "    return Endpoint.model_json_schema()", "explanation": "`BaseModel.schema()` is deprecated in v2; `model_json_schema()` is the replacement with the same output."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/docs.py:19:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return Endpoint.schema_json(indent=2)", "replace": "    return json.dumps(Endpoint.model_json_schema(), indent=2)", "explanation": "`BaseModel.schema_json()` is deprecated in v2. Equivalent is `json.dumps(Model.model_json_schema(), ...)`. The schema is plain JSON-compatible data, so no custom encoder is needed."}], "notes": "Four edits cover all three findings. The import edit has no finding id of its own; it only adds `json` and `ConfigDict` for the changes above. `Field(..., description=...)` and `List[str]` are valid in Pydantic v2 and were left unchanged. The `schema_json` replacement uses `json.dumps` on `model_json_schema()` because the v1 `schema_json` was just `json.dumps(self.schema(), ...)`. Edits don't overlap and are applied in order."}
